Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Scratch Build Remote Preflight Producer Design

@ [design_uuid] d762e7c4-f8da-4cce-86e1-0f1cf7544ec9
@ [source_uuid] fa3dbac1-04b8-4f10-a8a4-bb382bf1201f
@ [canonical_uuid] 935e020f-8c6f-49e4-b355-63eabd3b778b
@ [predecessor_bookend] 047674f26b4f9cb576fd93524d710d91e0e48b51

& [Problem]
  + the published observation compiler binds the result of one completed call but does not preserve the executable identity exact ordered argument atoms configured timeout or exact retained streams that produced that result
  + an effectful adapter implemented directly against that form could drift at the process boundary while still constructing a structurally valid downstream observation

& [Design]
  + compile a strict producer plan from the published request plan and effect program plus one supplied lowercase executable SHA256
  + fix native OpenSSH path transport options target and a UTF-16LE Base64 PowerShell probe payload that reads only the pinned listener and model coordinates and emits one canonical self-digested probe form
  + seal a strict process record that repeats plan identity executable and ordered argv and retains exact UTF-8 stdout and stderr with derived byte hashes timeout exit truncation call and effect accounting
  + compile the existing remote-preflight observation only when the process record replays exactly and stdout is exactly the embedded canonical probe form
  + provide canonical machine forms and a fresh-process verifier CLI without an effectful spawn path

& [Delineation]
  + inside is pure Rust plan and payload compilation Base64 encoding serialization digesting supplied process-record validation correspondence compilation CLI file ingress and provider-free tests
  + boundary is a future separately governed adapter that hashes the local executable performs at most one call under an independently admitted commission and writes the actual process record
  + outside is process spawning clock capture network SSH contact EVO-X2 state provider access transfer install build retrieval cleanup retry fallback remote machines FPGA Minecraft and autonomous work

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + constructive path closes executable-to-observation correspondence with deterministic byte-identical reconstruction
  + adversarial path refuses executable hash path argv order payload timeout stream exit truncation call accounting nested probe raw bytes canonical JSON and digest drift

& [DataDesign]
  + producer plan carries upstream request plan program and compiler commits target transport executable identity exact argv timeout stream caps zero provider-request budget one-call and one-effect maxima nonauthorizing disposition and self digest
  + process record carries producer-plan identity repeated executable and argv exact retained streams their byte identities duration completion outcome embedded probe accounting evidence class and self digest
  + verification carries only replayed identities configured and observed bounds and zero authority claims

& [FeatureRequirementSupport]
  + executable and argument pinning support the adversarial workspace and host-policy gates
  + raw retained streams and nested-probe replay support auditable live evidence
  + timeout caps and exact accounting support the one-contact stop boundary

& [ThreatReview]
  + argument-vector flattening is refused by retaining ordered atoms and comparing them to a deterministically regenerated vector
  + stdout substitution is refused by byte equality with the canonical embedded probe and independent byte count and SHA256
  + timeout truncation nonzero exit stderr or extra-call ambiguity is refused before downstream observation compilation
  + the plan remains nonauthorizing so mock success cannot silently become live-contact authority

& [PhaseDecision]
  + implement and mock-verify this producer contract provider-free and host-free under the published compiler bookend
  + publish and immediately bookend it before separately deciding whether a live one-contact adapter or invocation is eligible
